{
  "title": "Build Local Investor Pipeline for East Austin Boutique Hotel",
  "content": "## Plan Overview\n\nBuild a complete investor pipeline for a $2.4M pre-seed raise (boutique hotel + restaurant/bar in East Austin). The plan has four parallel research/creation tracks that feed into a final synthesis and delivery step.\n\n### Tracks:\n1. **Investor Database** - Research and compile Texas angel groups, hospitality investors, community investors, and connectors across Austin, Dallas, and Houston\n2. **Outreach Templates** - Create cold email, warm intro request, and follow-up sequence templates tailored to hospitality/real estate investors\n3. **Google Sheets CRM** - Build a lightweight pipeline tracker with stages, contact fields, meeting scheduler, and follow-up reminders\n4. **Meeting Cadence Framework** - Design a 3-meetings/week Tues-Thurs rhythm with prep checklists and follow-up workflows\n\nAll four tracks converge into a final synthesis task that packages everything into a unified, actionable investor pipeline playbook.",
  "tasks": [
    {
      "goal": "Research and compile a comprehensive Texas investor database: (1) Austin angel groups and syndicates (Central Texas Angel Network, Austin Angel Network, Techstars Austin alumni, Capital Factory investors), (2) Dallas/Houston angel groups (DFW Capital, Houston Angel Network, etc.), (3) Hospitality-focused investors (Creation Equity, Outpost Capital, Ohana RE, Flying Aca Capital, Vandelay Hospitality investors, hotel-focused PE/family offices), (4) Community/impact investors in Austin (East Austin development stakeholders, community development financial institutions), (5) Key connectors (commercial RE brokers, hospitality attorneys, Austin Chamber of Commerce contacts, restaurant/hotel operators who could intro). For each entry include: name, organization, focus areas, check size if known, location, contact method (LinkedIn/email/event), and relevance score (1-5). Produce a structured table/spreadsheet-ready format.",
      "tool_name": "spawn_sub_agent",
      "depends_on": []
    },
    {
      "goal": "Create a complete set of investor outreach templates for a pre-seed boutique hotel + restaurant/bar raise in East Austin ($3.2M total, $800K committed, seeking $2.4M). Produce: (1) Cold email template for angel groups/syndicates - emphasize approved city permits, land under contract, contractor ready, F&F momentum; (2) Cold email template for hospitality-focused investors - emphasize East Austin market, hotel+F&B concept, operator experience; (3) Warm intro request template - for asking connectors to make introductions; (4) Follow-up sequence (3 emails: Day 3, Day 7, Day 14) with escalating specificity; (5) LinkedIn connection request message (300 char limit); (6) Meeting confirmation/agenda email template; (7) Post-meeting thank you + next steps template. Each template should have [BRACKET] placeholders for personalization. Include subject line options for each email.",
      "tool_name": "spawn_sub_agent",
      "depends_on": []
    },
    {
      "goal": "Build a Google Sheets CRM template for investor pipeline tracking. Create the actual spreadsheet structure with these tabs: (1) 'Pipeline' - main tracker with columns: Investor Name, Organization, Type (Angel/Syndicate/HNW/Connector), Contact Info, Source, Outreach Date, Stage (Identified/Contacted/Responded/Meeting Scheduled/Meeting Done/Follow-Up/Committed/Passed), Next Action, Next Action Date, Meeting Date, Notes, Check Size Discussed, Warm Intro By, Priority (Hot/Warm/Cold); (2) 'Meeting Prep' - meeting date, investor name, research notes, key questions, ask amount, materials to bring, follow-up commitments; (3) 'Weekly Dashboard' - formulas/structure showing: meetings this week, pipeline by stage counts, total committed vs target ($2.4M), outreach velocity (emails sent/responses/meetings booked per week), conversion rates; (4) 'Outreach Log' - date, investor, channel (email/LinkedIn/phone/event), template used, response Y/N, response date; (5) 'Connectors' - name, relationship strength, investors they can intro to, last contact. Provide the complete column headers, sample data rows, conditional formatting rules, and key formulas. Output as a detailed specification that can be directly built in Google Sheets.",
      "tool_name": "spawn_sub_agent",
      "depends_on": []
    },
    {
      "goal": "Design a complete meeting cadence and weekly execution framework for an investor pipeline targeting 3 meetings/week on Tues-Thurs, with funding needed by ~December 2026 (mid-January operational). Include: (1) Weekly rhythm - Monday: research & outreach batch (send 10-15 personalized emails), review pipeline, prep for Tues-Thurs meetings; Tuesday/Wednesday/Thursday: 1 investor meeting each day (ideal time slots, location suggestions in Austin like coffee shops near East Austin site); Friday: follow-ups, update CRM, send thank-you notes, weekly reflection; (2) Ramp-up schedule - Week 1-2: build list, craft materials, start outreach; Week 3-4: first meetings begin; Week 5+: steady state 3/week; (3) Pre-meeting checklist (research investor, prepare deck section highlights, site photos/renderings, financial model talking points, specific ask); (4) Post-meeting protocol (same-day thank you, 48hr follow-up with requested materials, weekly touch base until decision); (5) Milestone targets by month (e.g., Month 1: 30 contacts, 8 meetings; Month 2: 50 contacts, 12 meetings, $500K new commitments); (6) Escalation strategies if pipeline stalls (pivot to events, expand to Colorado/Denver, engage placement agent). Factor in the Denver expansion angle as a conversation hook.",
      "tool_name": "spawn_sub_agent",
      "depends_on": []
    },
    {
      "goal": "Synthesize all four deliverables into a unified, actionable Investor Pipeline Playbook for the user. Combine: (1) the investor database from Task 0, (2) outreach templates from Task 1, (3) Google Sheets CRM specification from Task 2, and (4) meeting cadence framework from Task 3. Organize into a single coherent document with: Executive Summary (the raise: $2.4M needed, timeline, strategy), Section 1: Target Investor List (organized by tier/priority with recommended outreach order), Section 2: Outreach Templates (matched to investor types from the list), Section 3: CRM Setup Guide (step-by-step instructions to build the Google Sheet, with the complete spec), Section 4: Weekly Execution Playbook (the cadence framework with specific first-week action items), Section 5: Quick-Start Checklist (the first 10 things to do tomorrow). Make it immediately actionable - the user should be able to start executing within 24 hours of receiving this.",
      "tool_name": "reasoning",
      "depends_on": [0, 1, 2, 3]
    }
  ],
